  "event_layout": "Opcode, six argument words, then state before scripted mutations. Facing records signed row/column deltas; owner records fresh row/column; bridge records the input index. Road records index, attempted direction, uint8 cached Facing result, opaque a2, finite double low/high. Move records index, attempted direction, finite double low/high; it has no extra DWORD argument.",
  "state_layout": "Arena and selected index; signed16 row/column fields; eight counts, eight probe and eight other raw waypoint DWORDs; eight FNV-1a32 fingerprints of complete queued paths. Probe index is fixed by the input, independent of later count mutations. Other index is 1 when probe is 0, otherwise 0, so these fields never alias.",
  "final_layout": "Raw function result, state, and two full-arena FNV-1a32 fingerprints. The state and region fingerprints are not literal full-byte trace comparisons.",
  "exact_cleanup_check": "Both original and native recorders capture the complete two-arena bytes after initialization and after every scripted boundary mutation. At function return they directly compare all arena bytes against the latest snapshot with only the final live arena/input-index four-byte count cleared when the initial count was nonzero. Empty cases require byte equality with initialization. This independently checks the final cleanup width and untouched path payload/guards; earlier boundary memory observations remain the stated fields and fingerprints.",
  "index_evidence": "Original MOV ECX,EAX at 0x454AE4 retains the input stack index. All five normal-return callee contracts preserve ECX. Subsequent calls use that index and final cleanup recomputes its 725-byte offset before loading fresh gameData at 0x454BE3 and clearing the count at 0x454BF1. Native cur_stack_index was uninitialized; it is replaced by the input index without a selected-index assumption.",
  "before_comparison": "All nine defined empty-path before cases match original/after in four profiles. The other 246 nonempty cases are excluded before because cur_stack_index is read uninitialized; 21 also overflow the old signed count arithmetic. This is not a claim that every out-of-capacity raw representation is inherently undefined. No patched-before nonempty oracle is used; original-after is primary for the repairs.",
  "direction_scope": "There are 241 cases with empty paths or Facing results in its actual 0..7 range, plus 14 explicitly conditional scripted Facing results outside that range. Those 14 observe default dispatch and raw/full-versus-byte forwarding; they do not claim the actual Facing helper returns those values or that real movement accepts them.",
  "path_scope": "Every conventional count 0..100 and 24 backed raw-count cases are covered. The original address is path base plus count*4 with 32-bit scaling and base addition. Raw count 0x40000001 aliases waypoint 0; nonzero 0x40000000 aliases the count word. Cases also cover 101/102 and their period aliases reading adjacent bytes, plus 0xFFFFFFFF reading four bytes before the path. The native fixture validates the resolved four-byte address against actual arena backing, without a capacity policy. PathWaypoint is four bytes; uint8 target minus signed16 source remains safe signed32.",
  "compile_diagnostic_policy": "Actual-after recorder uses Wall/Wextra/Werror and UBSan with only the existing packed-layout alignment exception. No uninitialized diagnostic exception is needed for the repaired body.",
  "evidence": "artifacts/readability/road-functions-20260906/batch-14/original-proof/raw-count-revision/ and test-audit/raw-count-revision/ (private evidence; public tests require only tracked code and fixtures). Initial 231-case evidence and the prior public pair remain preserved, with its cases and traces unchanged in this extension.",
  "limits": [
    "Five callee entries are scripted recording/mutation boundaries. The original 573 helper bytes with both original switch tables and the actual native helper body execute; real Facing, owner/bridge queries, Road policy, pathfinding, movement and rendering do not.",
    "The original adapter separately checks ECX=input index, EBP=opaque a2 and cached full EBX=Facing result where applicable. Road common forwarding observes only BL as a uint8 byte. No AP or selected-index semantics are invented.",
    "Game-state pointers are backed positive signed-low32 in two arenas with four valid stack slots each. Invalid pointers or indices, raw waypoint addresses outside the backed arenas and corrupt callee control flow are outside this proof. Raw counts are not rejected solely for exceeding typed capacity.",
    "Finite double bits include signed zero, subnormals and finite extremes. No NaN/infinity or floating-point-environment behavior is claimed.",
    "Callback mutations test fresh and cached caller state at explicit boundaries; they are not assertions that each mutation occurs in unmodified gameplay.",
    "The nonempty result is always0 and the path count is cleared even when all attempts fail. A boundary-test result does not establish arrival, visual fidelity, a runtime route or a campaign milestone."
  ]
}
